From b9a57104f089ae325177cc324def7175b144f273 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:08:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: expose typed chain tip progress without changing
 readable diagnostics

Convert UpdateTipLog to chain_tip_updated with numeric header version, height, work, transaction count, progress, cache bytes/coins/MiB and Unix block time, plus hash/date and explicit active/background role. Retain IBD rate-limit bypass; render the header bit pattern and floating precision on the logger thread. No consensus, chainstate or wallet behavior changes.

Scripted diff commands (ast-grep-py==0.51.0):
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --root . --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/chain-tip-progress.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/tip-applied.json --apply
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/test_convert.py
python3 test/lint/lint-log-events.py src/validation.cpp
Explicit support adjustments: eleven appended registry fields and progress comment, recorded in catalog. Focused functional regression added; runtime gate pending resource grant. Dry-run idempotence produces an empty diff.
